# Which is the tallest mountain on Earth?
subtitle: "Everest is the highest, but is it the tallest? Guess, then watch Mauna Kea rise from the sea floor and meet the summit closest to the stars."

## Which is the tallest mountain on Earth?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Everest
      - Mauna Kea
    values:
      - [8849, 4207]
      - [8849, 10210]
    stage: 0
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 13000
    y_label: Metres
    box:
      x: 140
      'y': 215
      w: 470
      h: 430
sources:
    - id: noaa
      title: What is the highest point on Earth as measured from Earth's center?
      authors: US National Ocean Service (NOAA)
      year: 2024
      url: https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/highestpoint.html
      finding: Chimborazo's summit is the point farthest from Earth's centre, about 2 km farther out than Everest's, because Earth bulges at the equator
    - id: gwr
      title: Tallest mountain
      authors: Guinness World Records
      year: 2024
      url: https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/tallest-mountain
      finding: Mauna Kea rises about 10,210 m from its base on the Pacific floor, 4,205 m of it above sea level

    text above_sea "above sea" #b5482e x 297 y 575 font_size 30 hidden true
    text seafloor "from sea floor" #2f6b8f cites ["gwr"] x 532 y 628 font_size 30 hidden true
    ellipse earth #2f6b8f x 810 y 390 rx 145 ry 118 hidden true
    dot core at.canvas [810,390] hidden true
    path equator dashed #8f887c points [[665,390],[955,390]] style.stroke_width 2 hidden true
    path r_chim #b5482e points [[810,390],[955,390]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    text chim_l "Chimborazo" #b5482e cites ["noaa"] x 790 y 640 font_size 38 hidden true
    path r_ev thick #8f887c points [[810,390],[948,420]] hidden true
    text ev_l "Everest" #8f887c x 850 y 440 font_size 28 hidden true
    text plus "+2 km out" #b5482e cites ["noaa"] x 805 y 582 font_size 32 hidden true
    text bulge "equator" #8f887c x 740 y 362 font_size 30 hidden true

    card title "Which mountain is tallest?"

Which is the tallest mountain on Earth?
    draw axes

Everest is the highest: its summit stands 8,849 metres above the sea.
    draw bar_1 above_sea

    quiz "Measured from its foot to its summit, which mountain is tallest?"
        right: Mauna Kea, in Hawaii: from its foot on the sea floor, it rises about ten thousand two hundred metres.
        wrong: Think of where a mountain's foot can hide.
        * Everest
        * K2
        + Mauna Kea
        * Kilimanjaro

Above the waves, Mauna Kea is only about 4,200 metres.
    draw bar_2

But its foot lies some six thousand metres down, on the floor of the Pacific.
    animate stage 1 duration 2.5

Counted from there, it beats Everest by more than a kilometre.
    draw seafloor

And there is a third champion: Chimborazo, a volcano in Ecuador.
    draw earth core equator

The Earth bulges at the equator, and Chimborazo sits almost on it.
    draw r_chim chim_l bulge

So its summit is the point farthest from Earth's centre,
    draw r_ev ev_l

about two kilometres farther out than Everest's.
    draw plus

But the tallest of them all is mostly underwater.
    highlight bar_2
---
